From 71877a6223161ff0cee78a3a7e5a9edf2a48e86d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "David C. Manuelda" <StormByte@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:55:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] quantize: multiply negative scalefactor adjustments instead
 of shifting

The subblock gain adjustment explicitly takes this path when the adjusted
scalefactor s is negative. Shifting that signed value left to calculate
the gain is undefined.

Multiply by the positive scale factor instead. scalefac_scale is 0 or 1,
and s in this branch is bounded below by the preceding adjustment, so
the product is representable and preserves the intended gain.

Reproduced with UBSan during the existing MP3 audio-cover test.
---
 libmp3lame/quantize.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libmp3lame/quantize.c b/libmp3lame/quantize.c
index f29ed88..39ffe23 100644
--- a/libmp3lame/quantize.c
+++ b/libmp3lame/quantize.c
@@ -895,7 +895,7 @@ inc_subblock_gain(const lame_internal_flags * const gfc, gr_info * const cod_inf
 
             scalefac[sfb] = 0;
             {
-                int const gain = 210 + (s << (cod_info->scalefac_scale + 1));
+                int const gain = 210 + s * (1 << (cod_info->scalefac_scale + 1));
                 amp = IPOW20(gain);
             }
             j += width * (window + 1);
